SUMMARY:🍽 Beef Chili + Cornbread
DESCRIPTION:Cook time: 60 min\n\nDouble batch — freeze half\n\nMakes great leftovers. JIFFY cornbread muffins bake in 15 min. Double batch and freeze half the chili.\n\nIngredients:\n• 1.5 lb – 73% Lean / 27% Fat Ground Beef\, 1 lb\n• 2 can – Great Value Light Red Kidney Beans\, 15.5 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Pinto Beans\, 15.5 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Crushed Tomatoes with Tomato Puree\, 28 oz\n• 1 can – Great Value Tomato Paste\, 6 oz\n• 2 pkt – Great Value Mild Chili Seasoning Mix\, 1 oz\n• 2 box – "JIFFY" Corn Muffin Mix\, 8.5 oz\n• 0.25 carton – Great Value Large White Eggs\, 18 ct (for cornbread)\n• 0.25 gal – Great Value Whole Vitamin D Milk (for cornbread)\n• 1 bag – Great Value Fiesta Blend Shredded Cheese\, 8 oz\n• 0.5 tub – Great Value Light Sour Cream\, 16 oz
